name: Check an exact edited context and preserve history across source changes
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR NODE_OPTIONS
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_MODEL=openai-codex:gpt-5.5
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_check.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: use sast
submit: options sast:scan
submit: set taskMode manual
submit: set tasks secret-scan
submit: scan batch
require-live-snap: 20 PLAN A STUDY | study
keys: Down Down Down Enter Down Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Operator-owned fixture overview | edited-context
expect: c check
expect: Space actions
keys: Space
require-live-snap: 20 CONTEXT ACTIONS | actions
resize: 160x48
live-snap: actions-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: actions-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: actions-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: actions-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: actions-40x12
keys: Down Down Down Down Down Down
require-live-snap: 20 ▸ Tab Read complete document | final-action-40x12
ask: Are all seven context actions reachable at each size, with a clear selected action and working keyboard/back controls at 40x12?
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 CHOOSE STUDY CONTEXT | browser-40x12
expect: c check
expect: Space actions
ask: Do narrow context controls expose source checking and the complete actions menu without clipping, while retaining the selected context?
resize: 120x36
keys: Space Down Down Enter
require-live-snap: 30 Enter inspects the saved check | saved-check
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_check.py @TMP_TARGET @ART saved
ask: Does checking save an inactive revision with an honest structural verdict and explicit inspection/use steps, while preserving the original context, active context and source?
keys: a
require-live-snap: 20 Inspect this exact revision | use-before-inspection
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Operator-owned fixture overview | inspected-check
keys: a
require-live-snap: 20 Context selected for this study | selected-check
keys: L
require-live-snap: 30 Draft ready | finite-plan
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_check.py @TMP_TARGET @ART plan
keys: Enter Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Operator-owned fixture overview | reopened-check
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_check.py @TMP_TARGET @ART dirty
keys: c
require-live-snap: 30 source content changed | dirty-stop
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_check.py @TMP_TARGET @ART dirty-stopped
ask: Does a same-SHA content change visibly stop checking, preserve historical context and publish no new checked revision or jobs?
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 CHOOSE STUDY CONTEXT | dirty-context-kept
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_check.py @TMP_TARGET @ART sha
keys: c
require-live-snap: 30 source revision changed | sha-stop
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_check.py @TMP_TARGET @ART sha-stopped
ask: Does a new SHA with identical content stop rebinding too, and keep the earlier source reference without claiming a fix?
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 CHOOSE STUDY CONTEXT | historical-context-kept
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME NO_COLOR=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_MODEL=openai-codex:gpt-5.5
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
paste-file: @ART/resume-command.txt
keys: Enter
nav-mode:
keys: a
require-live-snap: 20 PLAN A STUDY | recovered-study
keys: Down Down Down Enter Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Operator-owned fixture overview | recovered-context
expect: Source drift at inspection: SHA changed
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_check.py @TMP_TARGET @ART plan
ask: Does a fresh no-color process recover the exact checked historical revision for the saved unapproved three-pass plan, with source drift disclosed and all work unstarted?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
